{"content_hash": "3cd1efeb5cfe46be", "version_id": 633, "article_id": 64, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "Sudan: 72 gold miners killed in air strikes near Egypt border", "title_zh": "苏丹：埃及边境附近空袭致72名淘金者死亡", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqy43vrk8wv8o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1621837593522-eae4fc6a9f17?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8N3x8ZG96ZW5zJTIwZ29sZCUyMHByb3NwZWN0b3JzfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE3NjYxMzJ8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Kanchanara on Unsplash", "author": "Kanchanara", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@kanchanara?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/silver-and-black-round-pendant-necklace-tayj2w_LCHI?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(69, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(107, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "8fb5b734dbc5"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-12", "word_count": 182, "reading_minutes": 0.9, "lead": "A rights group says at least 72 gold miners have been killed in air strikes in Sudan. The attacks happened near the border with Egypt, and no one has claimed responsibility yet.", "lead_zh": "一个人权组织称，苏丹发生的空袭导致至少72名淘金者死亡。袭击发生在与埃及接壤的边境地区，目前尚无人宣称负责。", "preview": "Emergency Lawyers, a group based in Khartoum, reported that jets targeted miners in Sudan's River Nile state on Saturday. The miners were wo", "preview_zh": "位于喀土穆的“紧急律师”组织报告称，周六战机袭击了苏丹尼罗河州的矿工。这些矿工当时在热门金矿点工作。到目前为止，埃及和苏丹实际掌权者均未对此事发表评论。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 621, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/64/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 70.85, "size_bytes": 428976, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 206, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@f606c78/content/data/versions/633.json", "paragraphs": ["Emergency Lawyers, a group based in Khartoum, reported that jets targeted miners in Sudan's River Nile state on Saturday. The miners were working at popular gold mining sites. So far, neither Egypt nor Sudan's de facto leaders have commented on the attacks.", "The group said the strikes may be war crimes because they deliberately targeted unarmed civilians. It also warned that the death toll is provisional and could rise. A survivor told the Sudan Tribune that many more people were injured, so the real number may be much higher.", "Eyewitnesses said the attack started around 6 a.m. local time, when aircraft fired more than five missiles at the miners' camps. The missiles destroyed the camps and pits, with people still inside. This follows similar accusations against Egypt in June, which Egypt denies.", "Gold is at the centre of tensions along the border. Sudan's civil war has led to a surge in artisanal mining, where civilians use simple tools without official permission. Egypt says it has seized 86 tonnes of gold ore and equipment as it tries to stop illegal mining and smuggling."], "paragraphs_zh": ["位于喀土穆的“紧急律师”组织报告称，周六战机袭击了苏丹尼罗河州的矿工。这些矿工当时在热门金矿点工作。到目前为止，埃及和苏丹实际掌权者均未对此事发表评论。", "该组织表示，这些袭击可能构成战争罪，因为它们故意针对手无寸铁的平民。它还警告说，死亡人数只是暂时的，可能还会上升。一名幸存者告诉《苏丹论坛报》，还有更多人受伤，因此真实数字可能要高得多。", "目击者称，袭击发生在当地时间早上6点左右，飞机向矿工营地发射了五枚以上导弹。导弹摧毁了营地和矿坑，里面还有人。此前6月曾发生针对埃及的类似指控，但埃及予以否认。", "黄金是边境紧张局势的核心。苏丹内战导致手工采矿激增，平民在没有官方许可的情况下使用简单工具采矿。埃及表示，在试图阻止非法采矿和走私的过程中，已查获86吨金矿石和设备。"], "body": "Emergency Lawyers, a group based in Khartoum, reported that jets targeted miners in Sudan's River Nile state on Saturday. The miners were working at popular gold mining sites. So far, neither Egypt nor Sudan's de facto leaders have commented on the attacks.\n\nThe group said the strikes may be war crimes because they deliberately targeted unarmed civilians. It also warned that the death toll is provisional and could rise. A survivor told the Sudan Tribune that many more people were injured, so the real number may be much higher.\n\nEyewitnesses said the attack started around 6 a.m. local time, when aircraft fired more than five missiles at the miners' camps. The missiles destroyed the camps and pits, with people still inside. This follows similar accusations against Egypt in June, which Egypt denies.\n\nGold is at the centre of tensions along the border. Sudan's civil war has led to a surge in artisanal mining, where civilians use simple tools without official permission. Egypt says it has seized 86 tonnes of gold ore and equipment as it tries to stop illegal mining and smuggling.", "body_zh": "位于喀土穆的“紧急律师”组织报告称，周六战机袭击了苏丹尼罗河州的矿工。这些矿工当时在热门金矿点工作。到目前为止，埃及和苏丹实际掌权者均未对此事发表评论。\n\n该组织表示，这些袭击可能构成战争罪，因为它们故意针对手无寸铁的平民。它还警告说，死亡人数只是暂时的，可能还会上升。一名幸存者告诉《苏丹论坛报》，还有更多人受伤，因此真实数字可能要高得多。\n\n目击者称，袭击发生在当地时间早上6点左右，飞机向矿工营地发射了五枚以上导弹。导弹摧毁了营地和矿坑，里面还有人。此前6月曾发生针对埃及的类似指控，但埃及予以否认。\n\n黄金是边境紧张局势的核心。苏丹内战导致手工采矿激增，平民在没有官方许可的情况下使用简单工具采矿。埃及表示，在试图阻止非法采矿和走私的过程中，已查获86吨金矿石和设备。", "text": "Emergency Lawyers, a group based in Khartoum, reported that jets targeted miners in Sudan's River Nile state on Saturday. The miners were working at popular gold mining sites. So far, neither Egypt nor Sudan's de facto leaders have commented on the attacks. The group said the strikes may be war crimes because they deliberately targeted unarmed civilians. It also warned that the death toll is provisional and could rise. A survivor told the Sudan Tribune that many more people were injured, so the real number may be much higher. Eyewitnesses said the attack started around 6 a.m. local time, when aircraft fired more than five missiles at the miners' camps. The missiles destroyed the camps and pits, with people still inside. This follows similar accusations against Egypt in June, which Egypt denies. Gold is at the centre of tensions along the border. Sudan's civil war has led to a surge in artisanal mining, where civilians use simple tools without official permission. Egypt says it has seized 86 tonnes of gold ore and equipment as it tries to stop illegal mining and smuggling.", "vocab": [{"word": "prospector", "pos": "noun", "zh": "淘金者，勘探者", "note": "指寻找金矿等资源的人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "air strike", "pos": "noun", "zh": "空袭", "note": "常用短语，指从空中发动的攻击", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "rights group", "pos": "noun", "zh": "人权组织", "note": "关注人权问题的团体", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "de facto", "pos": "adj", "zh": "实际上的", "note": "拉丁语，指事实上但未必合法的", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "provisional", "pos": "adj", "zh": "临时的，暂定的", "note": "常用来描述初步数据", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "war crime", "pos": "noun", "zh": "战争罪", "note": "违反国际法的严重罪行", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "artisanal mining", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "手工采矿", "note": "使用简单工具的小规模采矿", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "smuggling", "pos": "noun", "zh": "走私", "note": "非法运输货物", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "surge", "pos": "noun", "zh": "激增", "note": "突然的大幅增加", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "seize", "pos": "verb", "zh": "查获，扣押", "note": "官方强制拿走物品", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Dozens of gold prospectors killed in strikes on Egypt-Sudan border, rights group says", "summary_original": "Neither Egypt nor Sudan has commented on the alleged strikes on an artisanal mining camp on Saturday.", "body_original": "Dozens of gold prospectors killed in strikes on Egypt-Sudan border, rights group says\nBy\nAleks Phillips\nPublished\n3 hours ago\nAt least 72 civilians who had been prospecting for gold in a border region of Sudan have been killed in air strikes, a regional rights group says.\nEmergency Lawyers, based in the Sudanese capital, Khartoum, said jets targeted the so-called artisanal miners at a popular gold mining sites in Sudan's River Nile state on Saturday.\nNeither the Egyptian government nor the de facto Sudanese authorities have so far commented.\nCairo has previously faced accusations of deadly strikes on gold prospectors as part of a crackdown on illicit activity along its southern border.\nEmergency Lawyers noted the previous alleged attacks and said they represented not only a violation of Sudan's sovereign territory but demonstrated the government's lack of control over the region.\n\"The deliberate targeting of unarmed civilians violates international humanitarian law and the right to life,\" it said in a statement on Sunday. \"These acts may constitute war crimes.\"\nIt noted that its death toll was provisional and could rise.\nThe Paris-based Sudan Tribune reported that the death toll could far exceed the number reported by Emergency Lawyers, citing a survivor of Saturday's attack who said many more people had been injured.\nEyewitnesses said the attack began around 06:00 local time (04:00 GMT), with the aircraft firing more than five missiles directly at the miners' camps, destroying them and excavation pits with people still inside, the newspaper wrote.\nThe Sudan Tribune reported claims in June that Egyptian forces had used drones and artillery to target artisanal mining sites in the same region, killing several, after sporadic incidents of Egyptian border guards of burning equipment, torching temporary shelters, and firing live ammunition to disperse mine workers.\nDays later, Egypt's border agency announced that it and the military had begun a sweeping security campaign along the border to foil illegal migration, drug smuggling and illegal mining.\nAt the same time, Sudan's de facto leader announced an investigation into the alleged strikes, which were said to have killed dozens.\nGold lies at the core of the border tensions.\nSudan's ongoing civil war has led to a surge in artisanal mining - an often risky practice conducted by civilians with rudimentary tools and without official permission - particularly in remote areas near its borders.\nGold-rich areas such as those in River Nile state lie along porous borders in terrain historically associated with cross-border smuggling routes, with artisanally mined gold potentially feeding into those channels.\nEgypt's border force said in June that it had seized 86 tonnes of gold ore along with amateur prospecting equipment.\nArtisanal mining has also reportedly continued in Sudan's conflict zones and smuggled gold may be a source of income for armed insurgent groups.\nThis has raised concerns of illicit Sudanese gold undermining the legitimate Egyptian gold market.\nRelated topics\nSudan\nEgypt\nAfrica\nMining\nMore on this story\nA simple guide to what is happening in Sudan\nPublished\n13 November 2025", "fetched_at": "2026-10-12T00:48:50.607058", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Emergency", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.75, "sm": 100, "em": 750, "cs": 0, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Lawyers", "s": 0.762, "e": 1.237, "sm": 762, "em": 1237, "cs": 10, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": ",", "s": 1.237, "e": 1.4, "sm": 1237, "em": 1400, "cs": 17, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "a", "s": 1.4, "e": 1.487, "sm": 1400, "em": 1487, "cs": 19, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "group", "s": 1.5, "e": 1.762, "sm": 1500, "em": 1762, "cs": 21, "ce": 26, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "based", "s": 1.775, "e": 2.075, "sm": 1775, "em": 2074, "cs": 27, "ce": 32, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "in", "s": 2.087, "e": 2.175, "sm": 2087, "em": 2175, "cs": 33, "ce": 35, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "Khartoum", "s": 2.188, "e": 2.788, "sm": 2187, "em": 2787, "cs": 36, "ce": 44, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": ",", "s": 2.788, "e": 3.125, "sm": 2787, "em": 3125, "cs": 44, "ce": 45, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "reported", "s": 3.125, "e": 3.575, "sm": 3125, "em": 3575, "cs": 46, "ce": 54, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "that", "s": 3.587, "e": 3.737, "sm": 3587, "em": 3737, "cs": 55, "ce": 59, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "jets", "s": 3.75, "e": 4.062, "sm": 3750, "em": 4062, "cs": 60, "ce": 64, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "targeted", "s": 4.075, "e": 4.55, "sm": 4075, "em": 4550, "cs": 65, "ce": 73, "si": 0}, 